            "url": "https://www.axios.com/2019/05/13/trump-vladimir-putin-xi-jinping-russia-china",
            "title": "Trump says he will meet Russia's Putin and China's Xi at G20 summit",
            "snippets": [
              "Both meetings will be highly anticipated in the wake of the Mueller report and collapsed trade talks with China.\n\nOn",
              "# Trump says he will meet Putin and Xi at G20 summit\nAdd Axios on Google\n\nTrump\n\nPhoto: Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images\n\nPresident Trump told reporters Monday that he will meet with Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping at the G20 Summit on June 28 and 29 in Osaka, Japan",
              "**Why it matters:** This will be the first time Trump will meet with Putin since the release of the Mueller report, and the first time he'll meet with Xi since U.S.-China trade talks collapsed, resulting in increased tariffs on $200 billion worth of Chinese goods and threats of retaliation. Trump also told reporters that he hasn't yet decided whether to go forward with new tariffs on $325 billion of Chinese goods, as he has previously threatened.",
              "{\"articleSection\":\"World\",\"datePublished\":\"2019-05-13T18:37:27.425870Z\",\"headline\":\"Trump says he will meet Putin and Xi at G20 summit\",\"dateModified\":\"2019-05-13T22:09:24.377339Z\",\"author\":[{\"name\":\"Zachary Basu\"}],\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"Axios\"},\"isAccessibleForFree\":false,\"hasPart\":{\"isAccessibleForFree\":false}}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2019/05/13/trump-says-he-will-meet-with-xi-and-putin-at-g20-summit.html",
            "title": "Trump says he will meet with Xi and Putin at G20 summit",
            "snippets": [
              "# Trump says he has not decided whether to put tariffs on remaining $325 billion in Chinese goods\n- President Donald Trump says he has not \"made that decision yet\" on whether to put tariffs on another $325 billion in Chinese goods.\n- Trump says China's latest round of retaliatory tariffs represent \"a very positive step.\"\n- Trump confirms he will meet with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin at the G-20 summit in Japan in late June.",
              "VIDEO 1:40 01:40\n\nTrump: Can't let China take advantage of US any longer\n\nPower Lunch\n\nPresident Donald Trump said the latest round of retaliatory tariffs announced by China on Monday puts the United States in a great position and represents \"a very positive step\" in the ongoing trade negotiations",
              "China retaliated Monday against President Donald Trump's latest shot in the trade war between the world's two largest economies. Beijing said it would hike tariffs on $60 billion in U.S. goods to as high as 25%.\n\n\"I love the position we're in,\" Trump said, adding, \"There can be some retaliation, but it can't be very substantial by comparison.\"",
              "Trump also confirmed that he plans to meet with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin at the G-20 summit in Japan in late June.\n\n\"We have the right to do [tariffs on] another $325 billion at 25% in additional tariffs\" on Chinese goods, Trump said, but he added, \"I have not made that decision yet.\"",
              "The economic conflict widened last week as the two sides struggled to strike a new trade agreement. Trump decided to increase the tariffs following what the U.S. called China's decision to renege on key parts of a developing deal. Equities markets fell Monday after the Chinese retaliated",
              "\"We had a deal with China, it was 95% of the way there,\" Trump said, \"and then my representatives ... they went to China, and they were told things [that were fully agreed to] we're not gonna get anymore, they're gonna unagree [sic] to them... we're not gonna get anymore. And I said 'Good, that's fine, put on the tariffs,'\" Trump recounted",
              "Trump also said he would use a portion of the revenues that will be paid by consumers buying Chinese goods under the new tariffs to help provide financial relief for farmers.\n\nTrump has aimed to use the tariffs to pressure China into a trade deal. He has pushed Beijing to address what he calls unfair trade practices such as intellectual property theft and massive trade deficits.",
              "{\"headline\":\"Trump says he has not decided whether to put tariffs on remaining $325 billion in Chinese goods\",\"dateCreated\":\"2019-05-13T18:24:51+0000\",\"datePublished\":\"2019-05-13T18:24:51+0000\",\"dateModified\":\"2019-05-13T20:38:18+0000\",\"author\":[{\"name\":\"Christina Wilkie\"},{\"name\":\"Jacob Pramuk\"}],\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"CNBC\",\"foundingDate\":\"1989-04-17\",\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.facebook.com/cnbc\",\"https://www.instagram.com/cnbc\",\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/cnbc\",\"https://twitter.com/cnbc\",\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNBC\",\"https://www.youtube.com/cnbc\"]},\"articleSection\":\"Politics\",\"keywords\":[\"cnbc\",\"Articles\",\"Donald J. Trump\",\"Donald Trump\",\"Sanctions and embargoes\",\"Breaking News: Politics\",\"U.S. Economy\",\"Trade\",\"Politics\",\"White House\",\"US: News\",\"US Economy\",\"source:tagname:CNBC US Source\"],\"video\":{\"description\":\"CNBC's Eamon Javers reports on President Donald Trump's comments to reporters at the White House on U.S.-China trade talks and a possible meeting with China's Xi Jinping at the G20 Summit.\",\"duration\":\"PT1M40S\",\"name\":\"Trump: Can't let China take advantage of US any longer\",\"uploadDate\":\"2019-05-13T18:23:41+0000\"}}"
            ]
